  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-EI phase V-PMU Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given the commitment of Oxfam US (OUS) and the Oxfam Regional Platform in Asia to promote justice in extractive sectors in Asia; and following the Oxfam 2020 modality, this grant proposal is to confirm the funding commitment from OUS to the Oxfam International (OI) Regional Platform in Asia with the support of Oxfam Netherlands (ONL) as an Executing Agency (EA) to help manage the grant proposal. This grant proposal#s main objective is to enable the Regional Extractive Industries (EI) Program Coordinator to fullfil his role to coordinate the implementation of country and regional partner grant proposals in order to deliver program outcomes and impacts.Specifically, for 1 April 2023- 31 March 2024, this project will enable EI regional program coordinator to fullfil his works:

1. Develop capacity of OIC and NGO partners to strategically and sustainably position EI and Natural Resource Governance program interventions to deliver impacts on protecting women rights and IPs rights  and improving CSO roles in EI Governance in Cambodia.

2. Offertechnical supports and oversight to Oxfam in Vietnam to implement the OUS invested projects related to EI and gender-EI to improve CSO roles in promoting gender justice, accountability and community rights protection (10%).

3. Offer some technical and managerialsupports and guidance to implement EI related projects in Timor Leste and Myanmar.

4. Support efforts to promote regional program coordination, and contribute  to the development of CLV strategies andOxfam Asia strategic review process.

5. Managing two EI regional projects in partnership with AIPP/AIPNEE and NTFP-EP.

6. Contribute to learning and knowledge sharing and offer inputs to EI global team discussion.</narrative>
  </description>
